     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br>On Thursday, June 25, 2015 at 7:47:28 AM UTC-4, Tareef Kawaf wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Adding Winston&#39;s response to the shiny-discuss list<div><br></div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8000001907349px\">The nearPoints() function itself won&#39;t work with bar graphs, since it uses both the x and y distance. But you can use the x position and calculate yourself which bar the mouse is over. Here&#39;s an example from <a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/plot-interaction-advanced.html\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/plot-interaction-advanced.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398030554000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0w-kW46GTHRX2krvGZiGfl\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/plot-interaction-advanced.html</a>, adapted slightly to have bar graphs generated by ggplot2:<div><br></div><div><div><br></div><div>library(ggplot2)</div><div><br></div><div>ui &lt;- fluidPage(</div><div>  fluidRow(</div><div>    plotOutput(&quot;plot1&quot;, height = 300, width = 300,</div><div>      click = &quot;plot1_click&quot;,</div><div>    )</div><div>  ),</div><div>  verbatimTextOutput(&quot;x_value&quot;),</div><div>  verbatimTextOutput(&quot;selected_rows&quot;)</div><div>)</div><div><br></div><div>server &lt;- function(input, output) {</div><div>  output$plot1 &lt;- renderPlot({</div><div>    ggplot(ToothGrowth, aes(supp)) + geom_bar(stat = &quot;bin&quot;)</div><div>  })</div><div><br></div><div>  # Print the name of the x value</div><div>  output$x_value &lt;- renderPrint({</div><div>    if (is.null(input$plot1_click$x)) return()</div><div><br></div><div>    lvls &lt;- levels(ToothGrowth$supp)</div><div>    lvls[round(input$plot1_click$x)]</div><div>  })</div><div>  </div><div>  # Print the rows of the data frame which match the x value</div><div>  output$selected_rows &lt;- renderPrint({</div><div>    if (is.null(input$plot1_click$x)) return()</div><div>    </div><div>    keeprows &lt;- round(input$plot1_click$x) == as.numeric(ToothGrowth$supp)</div><div>    ToothGrowth[keeprows, ]</div><div>  })</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div>shinyApp(ui, server)</div></div><div><br></div><div>-Winston</div></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8000001907349px\"><div style=\"margin-top:5px;margin-bottom:5px\"><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(221,221,221);clear:both;line-height:6px;outline:none;width:20px;color:rgb(80,0,80);font-size:11px;background-color:rgb(241,241,241)\"></div></div></div><br>On Wednesday, June 24, 2015 at 11:47:07 AM UTC-4, SivaSankara Reddy Bommireddy wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">I am trying to use <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">nearPoints()</code> function in Shiny with bar-graphs(both basic and <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">ggplot</code>packages). But when the page is rendered, none of the <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">click, dbclick, hover</code> are not working with the bar-graphs.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">My aim is to show either a <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">dataTable</code> or <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">verbatimTextOutput</code> (containing the rows of the clicked bar) when a bar on the bar-graph is clicked. I can do the above mentioned operations on a scattered plot but not on a bar graph.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">The examples mentioned in the <a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/selecting-rows-of-data.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/selecting-rows-of-data.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398030554000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0xVmd-NhaYqLnniovxsvbm\">Shiny documentation page</a> only showed the scattered plots examples. I just want to know if the <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courie